{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L --fail --max-time 20 -sS https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/docs/maintenance_use/ | rg -n -i 'efetch|vcv|allele|api|variation|accession' | head -160\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L --fail --max-time 20 -sS https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/docs/maintenance_use/ | rg -n -i 'efetch|vcv|allele|api|variation|accession' | head -160\"","aggregated_output":"26:        <meta name=\"author\" content=\"ClinVar\" /><meta name=\"ncbi_app\" content=\"entrez\" /><meta name=\"ncbi_db\" content=\"clinvar\" /><meta http-equiv=\"Cache-control\" content=\"no-cache\" /><meta name=\"description\" content=\"ClinVar archives and aggregates information about relationships among variation and human health.\" /><meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"variation, mutation, human, health, precision medicine, genetic testing, variant, database, disease, allele, genome\" /><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.6.0/css/all.min.css\" /><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/projects/clinvar/data/base.css\" /><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/projects/clinvar/data/clinvar_search.css\" /><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/projects/clinvar/data/clinvar_search.js\"></script>\n211:                            <div class=\"res_logo\"><h1 class=\"res_name\"><a href=\"/clinvar/\" title=\"ClinVar home\">ClinVar</a></h1><h2 class=\"res_tagline\">Relating variation to medicine</h2></div>\n265:                        <a href=\"/clinvar/docs/identifiers/\" class=\"usa-link  \"> Accessions and identifiers </a>\n282:                        <a href=\"/clinvar/docs/variation_report/\" class=\"usa-link  \"> VCV (variant) pages </a>\n325:<p><a href=\"#disclaimer\">Disclaimer</a> | <a href=\"#web\">Web Access</a> | <a href=\"#download\">Data for download</a> | <a href=\"#api\">APIs</a> | <a href=\"#releases\">Release cycle</a></p>\n371:<td>Links to the ClinVar VCV pages in the Summary section and links to the ClinVar RCV pages on the Clinical Significance tab on the RefSNP report</td>\n380:<td>Genes in which variation has been reported in ClinVar</td>\n385:<td>Human genes in which variation has been reported in ClinVar</td>\n388:<p>See variants in ClinVar in the Variation section</p>\n401:<td>Allelic variants accessioned in ClinVar</td>\n410:<td>Variation Viewer</td>\n412:<td>ClinVar link in the Allele information display</td>\n464:<span id=\"api\"></span></p>\n467:<h3 id=\"application-programming-interfac\">Application programming interface (API)</h3>\n470:<p>Data from ClinVar can be retrieved programmatically via several application programming interfaces (API). These include:</p>\n476:<p>As part of NCBI's Entrez system, ClinVar can be accessed by E-utilities, both via <a href=\"/books/NBK25501/\">web services</a> and a UNIX command line as <a href=\"/books/NBK179288/\">Entrez Direct</a>. The subset of functions ClinVar currently supports are esearch, esummary, elink, and efetch.</p>\n479:<p>The general approach is to use esearch to find the list of unique identifiers that return records of interest, and then use either esummary (to retrieve an overview of each of those records) or efetch (to retrieve the complete record), based on the identifiers returned by esearch.  esearch uses the same query language that you use interactively, so you can test your query on the web before automating as esearch.</p>\n502:<strong>find 500 records for the gene FGFR3, excluding variations that include multiple genes, by using the property <a href=\"/clinvar/docs/properties/\">\"single_gene\"</a>, and return results in the default XML format</strong></p><p>\n541:<td>Use efetch to retrieve the XML for one or more variation records (XML that is consistent with the VCV XML) based on their id(s). Note <code>rettype=vcv&amp;is_variationid</code></td>\n543:<a href=\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;is_variationid&amp;id=14206,41472&amp;from_esearch=true\">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;is_variationid&amp;id=14206,41472&amp;from_esearch=true</a>\n547:<td>Use efetch to retrieve the XML for the most recent version of a VCV accession. Note rettype=vcv\n550:<a href=\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;id=VCV000014206\">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;id=VCV000014206</a>\n554:<td>Use efetch to retrieve the XML for a specified version of a VCV accession. Note rettype=vcv\n557:<a href=\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;id=VCV000014206.1\">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=vcv&amp;id=VCV000014206.1</a>\n561:<td>Use efetch to retrieve the XML for the most recent version of an RCV accession. Note <code>rettype=clinvarset</code></td>\n563:<a href=\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=clinvarset&amp;id=RCV000000606\">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=clinvarset&amp;id=RCV000000606</a>\n567:<td>Use efetch to retrieve the XML for a specified version of an RCV accession. Note <code>rettype=clinvarset</code></td>\n569:<a href=\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=clinvarset&amp;id=RCV000000606.3\">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;rettype=clinvarset&amp;id=RCV000000606.3</a>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
